---@overload fun(...)
  ---@param groupData table #the group record handed to the provider's addGroup
  ---@return boolean, string #false plus a reason when the caller is not allow-listed, or when no doors provider is registered
---@overload
  ---@param data table #the group record; the key set is provider-defined and nothing here validates it
  ---@return boolean #registered or not; false on refusal
---@overload
function AddDoorGroup.server(groupData) end
function AddDoorGroup.client(data) end

---@overload fun(...)
  ---@param newDoorData table #the door record, handed to the provider unexamined
  ---@param internal any #a flag passed straight through and never read here 
-- Why `any`: a flag forwarded to the provider and never read by cis_libs, so nothing here can know what a provider makes of it
  ---@return boolean, string #false plus a reason when the caller is off Security.AuthorizedResources, or when no doors provider is registered
---@overload
  ---@param data table #the door record, forwarded unexamined to the doorsClient slot
  ---@return boolean #registered or not; false on refusal
---@overload
function AddDoorToSystem.server(newDoorData, internal) end
function AddDoorToSystem.client(data) end

--- Cis.sync.onDespawn(fn)
---@param fn function #a non-function is refused rather than stored
---@return boolean, string #true alone on success. The handler is called pcall'd as (key) and only when this client actually held something
--- realm: client
function AddSyncDespawnHandler(fn) end

--- Cis.sync.onSpawn(fn)
---@param fn function #a non-function is REFUSED rather than stored -- storing it is a nil call on the spawn path one step later
---@return boolean, string #true alone on success. Never a handle: there is no deregister. The handler is called pcall'd as (key, record, entity), and fires only after the generation check, so an entity created and immediately deleted never announces itself
--- realm: client
function AddSyncSpawnHandler(fn) end

--- Cis.streaming.animDict(name, timeout)
---@param name string #the dictionary NAME, not a hash -- RequestAnimDict takes a char*, and a hash is a type error the game answers by never loading
---@param timeout? integer #ms, default 5000
---@return string|nil, string|nil #the name, or nil plus a reason. THE ONLY KIND WITH AN EXISTENCE PROBE, so an invalid dictionary is refused immediately rather than after the whole timeout
--- realm: client
function AnimDict(name, timeout) end

