---@overload fun(...)
  ---@param src integer #a connected player id above 0; console and broadcast included, anything else refuses
  ---@param message string #the text; over 512 characters it is TRUNCATED, not refused
  ---@param kind? string #forwarded to the provider and the client event unvalidated
  ---@return boolean, string #true, or false plus a reason for a bad src, a disconnected player, or the rate limit
---@overload
  ---@param message any #the text, stringified on the native-feed path and passed through on the framework path 
-- Why `any`: stringified on the native-feed path and passed through untouched on the framework path, so the two disagree about what is legal and the union is the honest answer
  ---@param kind? any #forwarded verbatim as the second argument to ShowNotification 
-- Why `any`: forwarded verbatim to ShowNotification or the provider; this library assigns no vocabulary to it, so anything is a type this code cannot narrow
  ---@return any, string|nil #with a provider, every value it produced; with NO framework registered, nothing is returned at all -- not even nil 
-- Why `any`: the provider's own value, handed back as it came; there is no registered contract for this slot's result, so narrowing it would be inventing one
---@overload
function Notify.server(src, message, kind) end
function Notify.client(message, kind) end

--- Called by a product to show a notification to one client, without hardcoding the event name owned by this library. Answers `false, reason` for a src that is not a connected player, truncates a message past 512 characters, and allows 10 a second per (src, calling resource)
---@param src integer #a connected player id above 0
---@param message string #the text; over 512 characters it is truncated, not refused
---@param kind? string #forwarded to the client event unvalidated
---@return boolean, string #true once fired; false plus a reason for a bad src, a disconnected player, or the rate limit
--- realm: server
function NotifyClient(src, message, kind) end

--- Cis.player.on(key, cb). The cb cannot cross the boundary; use a net event
---@param key string #a listener key: ped, vehicle, seat, weapon, armed or aiming. NEVER type-checked here, and the same file lists the keys
---@param cb function #a non-function returns immediately with no subscription at all
---@return function|nil #the unsubscribe closure, in-realm only. A LISTENER ARGUMENT IS DROPPED across the boundary -- the teardown arrives and the listener never fires -- so gate on your own flag and drop it in onResourceStop
--- realm: client
function OnPlayerCache(key, cb) end

