  ---@param name string #a previously registered name, quoted in the refusal string
  ---@param ... ... #the unbounded tail, packed then forwarded whole
  ---@return boolean, any #true plus the handler's whole result list, so a nil in the middle survives; false plus a reason otherwise. Slot 1 is always the ok flag, never a handler value 
-- Why `any`: the handler's own result list, whose arity and types the handler alone decides
---@overload
  ---@param name string #a previously registered name
  ---@param ... ... #the unbounded tail, forwarded bare
  ---@return boolean, any #true plus the whole packed reply; false plus a reason otherwise, and it never raises 
