---@class Cis.waitFor
---@field since string 1.0.0
---@field realm "both"
---@param fn function #polled EVERY FRAME until it answers a value; false is treated as "not yet", so a predicate returning false for success has to say so in its return type
---@param msg? string #names WHICH wait timed out, and appears in the reason
---@param timeoutMs? number #default 10000. NaN and infinity are refused -- both would loop forever. 0 means poll once
---@return any, string|nil #the first value fn answered, or nil plus a reason. PURE: it runs in the consumer own VM with no export and no boundary. Timeout does not raise. 
-- Why `any`: the value is whatever fn returned, and this function cannot know that type
function Cis.waitFor(fn, msg, timeoutMs) end

